      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-data-shape-contract-view",
      "type": "port",
      "label": "View",
      "position": {
        "x": 40,
        "y": -460
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 280,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Bridge Data Shape Contract",
        "purpose": "Shared host-facing view for the bridge data-shape contract.",
        "titleSourceNodeId": "bridge-data-shape-contract-title",
        "typeSourceNodeId": "bridge-data-shape-contract-type",
        "audience": "Author",
        "status": "active",
        "svg": "<svg viewBox=\"0 0 220 160\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"100%\" height=\"100%\" preserveAspectRatio=\"xMidYMid meet\">\n  <defs>\n    <linearGradient id=\"shapeCard\" x1=\"0\" y1=\"0\" x2=\"1\" y2=\"1\">\n      <stop offset=\"0%\" stop-color=\"#fffdf7\"/>\n      <stop offset=\"100%\" stop-color=\"#dbeafe\"/>\n    </linearGradient>\n  </defs>\n  <rect x=\"22\" y=\"22\" width=\"176\" height=\"116\" rx=\"18\" fill=\"url(#shapeCard)\" stroke=\"#0f766e\" stroke-width=\"5\"/>\n  <rect x=\"42\" y=\"42\" width=\"52\" height=\"20\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#ccfbf1\" stroke=\"#0f766e\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <rect x=\"102\" y=\"42\" width=\"76\" height=\"20\" rx=\"10\" fill=\"#eff6ff\" stroke=\"#2563eb\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <rect x=\"42\" y=\"74\" width=\"136\" height=\"18\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#f8fafc\" stroke=\"#64748b\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <rect x=\"42\" y=\"102\" width=\"40\" height=\"18\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#bbf7d0\" stroke=\"#15803d\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <rect x=\"90\" y=\"102\" width=\"50\" height=\"18\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#ddd6fe\" stroke=\"#7c3aed\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n  <rect x=\"148\" y=\"102\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" rx=\"9\" fill=\"#e2e8f0\" stroke=\"#475569\" stroke-width=\"3\"/>\n</svg>",
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/ui-interaction/ui-view.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-data-shape-contract-skill",
      "type": "skill",
      "label": "Skill",
      "position": {
        "x": -1220,
        "y": -60
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 260,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "BridgeDataShapeContract",
        "body": "Define the canonical bridge node fields so focused-graph authority remains explicit, inspectable, and stable across authoring, rendering, creation, and runtime enforcement.",
        "category": "boundary",
        "authority": "normative",
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/skill-contract/skill.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-data-shape-contract-scope",
      "type": "scope",
      "label": "Scope",
      "position": {
        "x": -620,
        "y": -60
      },
      "width": 360,
      "height": 240,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Scope",
        "body": "Use this contract when storing bridge nodes, creating new bridge instances, migrating old bridge-like ports, validating bridge authority, or resolving bridge renderer and runtime behavior from graph data.",
        "conditions": [
          "A bridge node is created or edited.",
          "A port-in-bridge-mode is migrated to a real bridge node.",
          "Renderer code resolves target identity, grants, or scope from stored graph data.",
          "Runtime code checks whether a bridge grants create or runtime authority."
        ],
        "description": "Bridge scope is local to the focused graph. Bridges are not semantic-zoom content and are not part of normal browser presentation.",
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/skill-contract/scope.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-data-shape-contract-input",
      "type": "input",
      "label": "Input",
      "position": {
        "x": -20,
        "y": -60
      },
      "width": 360,
      "height": 240,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Input",
        "body": "A bridge node consumes a referenced target artifact plus explicit host-owned authority fields describing what the focused graph is allowed to do with that target.",
        "required": true,
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/skill-contract/input.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-data-shape-contract-output",
      "type": "output",
      "label": "Output",
      "position": {
        "x": 580,
        "y": -60
      },
      "width": 360,
      "height": 240,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Output",
        "body": "A valid bridge node stores target ref, resource kind, scope, and explicit grants in a stable canonical shape that both renderer and runtime can read without guessing.",
        "reversible": true,
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/skill-contract/output.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-data-shape-contract-rule",
      "type": "rule",
      "label": "Rule",
      "position": {
        "x": -20,
        "y": 320
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 250,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Rule",
        "body": "Store bridge authority explicitly. Renderer and runtime should read the same canonical shape rather than inferring grants from old port modes, labels, or target existence alone.",
        "severity": "high",
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/skill-contract/rule.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-data-shape-contract-guardrail",
      "type": "guardrail",
      "label": "Guardrail",
      "position": {
        "x": 580,
        "y": 320
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 250,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Guardrail",
        "body": "Do not split bridge truth across too many legacy fields. Compatibility fallbacks are acceptable, but the canonical shape must be singular and explicit.",
        "hardStop": true,
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/skill-contract/guardrail.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-data-shape-contract-failure",
      "type": "failure-mode",
      "label": "Failure Mode",
      "position": {
        "x": 1180,
        "y": 320
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 250,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Failure Mode",
        "body": "A weak bridge data shape scatters authority across `_bridge`, `target`, `authority`, and ad hoc labels. That makes bridges hard to inspect, migrate, and enforce consistently.",
        "response": "refuse",
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/skill-contract/failure-mode.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-data-shape-contract-procedure",
      "type": "procedure",
      "label": "Procedure",
      "position": {
        "x": 1180,
        "y": 700
      },
      "width": 420,
      "height": 250,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "title": "Procedure",
        "body": "Resolve the target ref first, stamp the canonical bridge object second, then mirror or derive any legacy fallback fields only as compatibility shims. New bridge authoring should write the canonical shape directly.",
        "steps": [
          "Read the host port authority; default new ports to navigate.",
          "Read the target exposure: named views, bridgeability, runtime capability, and default root behavior.",
          "Validate semantic meaning, direction, semantic type, multiplicity, and wildcard policy.",
          "Compute effective authority as the minimum of host authority, target exposure, and local policy.",
          "Filter the result to the allowed boundary behavior or refuse if no safe behavior remains."
        ],
        "classRef": "github://twilite-zone/public/library/classes/nodes/skill-contract/procedure.node-class.node"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-data-shape-schema-examples",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "9. Examples",
      "position": {
        "x": 1780,
        "y": -60
      },
      "width": 560,
      "height": 320,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## Examples\n\n**Valid:**\n- host.navigate_port -> target.root\n- host.consume_view -> target.port_view\n\n**Invalid (must fail):**\n- bridge authority inferred from a rendered card\n- runtime behavior granted because a target view happens to exist\n- incompatible semantic types connected without an explicit wildcard policy"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-data-shape-schema-migrations",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "10. Migration Notes",
      "position": {
        "x": 1780,
        "y": 700
      },
      "width": 560,
      "height": 300,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## Migration Notes\n\nDocument explicit, reversible evolution for:\n\n- authority ladder changes\n- semantic type renames\n- multiplicity changes\n- default root policy changes\n- boundary filtering behavior\n\nMigration notes must preserve portability and avoid silent authority escalation."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-data-shape-schema-human-notes",
      "type": "content",
      "label": "12. Human Notes",
      "position": {
        "x": -1820,
        "y": -60
      },
      "width": 560,
      "height": 280,
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": true,
      "data": {
        "content": {
          "kind": "markdown",
          "value": "## Human Notes\n\nUse this space for rationale, stewardship notes, and examples that help humans maintain the port API without weakening the normative boundary rules."
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "bridge-data-shape-contract-entity-port",
      "type": "import",
      "label": "Entity",
      "position": {
        "x": -868.7202021307858,
